#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD1011 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "Negative control for the single-expansion shape. Same minimal column set as the invalid twin - AVISITN is the only `*N`/`*C` match, so exactly one expansion exists and the rule EXECUTES; every row populates the primary AVISIT alongside its secondary, so neither arm holds and the rule stays silent. Do not add any further column ending in N or C: it would add an expansion."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AVISIT  type=Char
col AVISITN type=Num
---
